"The prognosis is influenced by several factors, including a preoperative PSA of 12 and an ISUP grade group 5 Gleason pattern (4+5) identified in the prostatectomy specimen. Contributing to risk are the pathological T3a stage and documented extraprostatic extension. Countervailing findings include negative surgical margins, no seminal vesicle invasion, absence of lymphovascular invasion, and no detected lymph node metastasis. A significant discrepancy exists between the biopsy finding (Gleason 0+0) and the prostatectomy specimen grade/stage. Missing information regarding postoperative PSA trajectory would be crucial for refining this prognosis. The current assessment is based on available surgical pathology data. The fixed estimated horizon is 51.41 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 41.13–61.69 months; its coverage has not been validated."
